1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,891
The Vienna Gambit starts with a pawn offer for speed.

2
00:00:03,971 --> 00:00:07,863
White brings the knight out before Black can settle.

3
00:00:07,943 --> 00:00:11,834
The f pawn hits the center and opens attacking lines.

4
00:00:11,914 --> 00:00:15,806
Black strikes back, but the e pawn keeps moving.

5
00:00:15,886 --> 00:00:19,777
White develops with tempo instead of defending the pawn.

6
00:00:19,857 --> 00:00:23,749
The bishops trade, and the center stays dangerously open.

7
00:00:23,829 --> 00:00:27,720
The lesson: initiative is compensation when every move attacks.
